{"id": "EUVD-2026-103630", "enisaUuid": "81afd46d-96b5-3b9a-8834-4fb586f2b59f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\neth: fbnic: Avoid rounding zero ring sizes\n\nroundup_pow_of_two() is undefined for zero. ethtool permits a zero ring\nsize to reach the driver, where the minimum-size check should reject it.\n\nLeave zero unchanged while rounding nonzero ring sizes. The minimum-size\ncheck then rejects zero deterministically without changing the established\nbehavior for other values.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/92c9f2ea634d92adff5403d231ebeda683c5685a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/491aa3167ae02f219cb2d2de6f4196d28dca03be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0160953d8eec75c3c55562158c46442ff1fd410b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pmrp-mw94-3ww9", "CVE-2026-98585"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08f2cb9d-bb89-343c-af7d-094265ba3779", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "2e5d1880-2ce4-3716-9325-ac266114b9c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "3f989404-a18d-3cc4-93d9-44e5a24d40de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "566641bc-d6a0-31a1-9b28-ae8316378c42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "74effce5-d4e3-3e03-ba60-3e10e9394b88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6cbf18a05c06090d867ef417a2a30b214d42d171 <491aa3167ae02f219cb2d2de6f4196d28dca03be"}, {"id": "9eba480c-8852-3335-bf6d-181f325bc4ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e3e7f3d6-11cf-3075-b54f-3db48b6bee3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux